<section class="headless" id="headless" aria-labelledby="headless-h">
  <p class="section-label" id="headless-h">Headless</p>
  <p class="block-intro">
    Automate tasks by running imza without the terminal UI: same tools, same
    permission system. Final output goes to stdout, diagnostics to stderr.
  </p>
  <div class="tui-panel command-panel" aria-label="Headless command examples">
    <pre
      class="command-body"><span class="t-prompt">$</span> imza --ask <span class="t-arg">"summarize the architecture of this repo"</span>

<span class="t-prompt">$</span> imza --session my-session --exec <span class="t-arg">"finish the TODOs in NOTES.md"</span>

<span class="t-prompt">$</span> imza --exec <span class="t-arg">"build and summarize the changes"</span> \
    --allow-dir ../shared-assets \
    --allow-cmd <span class="t-arg">"git status"</span> <span class="t-arg">"cmake --build"</span></pre>
    <p class="command-note">
      <code>--ask</code> runs one read-only Plan turn;
      <code>--exec</code> runs one Build turn. Unresolved approvals come back to the
      model as rejections, so grant only what the task needs.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .command-body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: clamp(0.72rem, 0.66rem + 0.3vw, 0.9rem);
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--fg);
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .command-note :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--focus);
    padding: 0.05em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 0.125rem;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .command-note {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    background: var(--focus);
  }
  .t-prompt {
    color: var(--hl-green);
  }
  .t-arg {
    color: var(--hl-blue);
  }
</style>
